== [1] git-diff-tree: anchors used by the lane's record-parsing family ==
-- --raw --
3441|TEXT:--raw
3442|TEXT:
3443|TEXT:Generate the diff in raw format.
3444|TEXT:This is the default.
3445|TEXT:
-- --name-only / --name-status --
3654|TEXT:--name-only
3655|TEXT:
3656|TEXT:Show only the name of each changed file in the post-image tree.
3657|TEXT:The file names are often encoded in UTF-8.
3658|TEXT:For more information see the discussion about encoding in the git-log[1]
3659|TEXT:manual page.
3660|TEXT:
3661|TEXT:--name-status
3662|TEXT:
3663|TEXT:Show only the name(s) and status of each changed file. See the description
3664|TEXT:of the --diff-filter option on what the status letters mean.
3665|TEXT:Just like --name-only the file names are often encoded in UTF-8.
3666|TEXT:
-- -r / -t --
4375|TEXT:-r
4376|TEXT:
4377|TEXT:Recurse into sub-trees.
4378|TEXT:
4379|TEXT:-t
4380|TEXT:
4381|TEXT:Show tree entry itself as well as subtrees.  Implies -r.
4382|TEXT:
-- --root --
4383|TEXT:--root
4384|TEXT:
4385|TEXT:When --root is specified the initial commit will be shown as a big
4386|TEXT:creation event. This is equivalent to a diff against the NULL tree.
4387|TEXT:
-- --no-commit-id --
4565|TEXT:--no-commit-id
4566|TEXT:
4567|TEXT:git diff-tree outputs a line with the commit ID when
4568|TEXT:applicable.  This flag suppresses the commit ID output.
4569|TEXT:
-- Raw output format --
5369|TEXT:Raw output format
5370|TEXT:
5371|TEXT:
5372|TEXT:The raw output format from git-diff-index, git-diff-tree,
5373|TEXT:git-diff-files and git diff --raw are very similar.
-- one line per changed file --
5400|TEXT:All the commands print one output line per changed file,
5401|TEXT:except git diff-files in the case of an unmerged file, which prints
5402|TEXT:both an "unmerged" and an "in-place edit" line.
